fragment:

  - The parameters should be generated by LLM according to the context.
- The explanation for each action should be generated by LLM according to the context in which that action was chosen (reason, sequence, etc.).
- "action_id" is not sequential identifier, it must match the number in parentheses of the chosen action.
Exemples:
SET_TEXT (3) == "action_id": "3"
CLICK (4) == "action_id": "4"
LONG_CLICK (2) == "action_id": "2"
BACK (5) == "action_id": "5"

Your response MUST follow this schema - a JSON object with the following structure:
{
  "actions": [
    {
      "action_id": "5",
      "action_text": "CLICK (5)",
      "params": {},  
      "explanation": "Why this action is included in the batch"
    },
    {
      "action_id": "2",
      "action_text": "SET_TEXT (2)",
      "params": {"text": "test@example.com"},
      "explanation": "Why this action logically follows the previous one"
    }
    // Additional related actions...
  ],
  "batch_explanation": "Overall explanation of why these actions form a logical batch"
}


Você também pode sugerir ações de click, ao analisar a imagem, passando as coordenadas que deseja:
{
  "actions": [
    {
      # TODO: definir como sera a acao custom ... cria outro tipo de acao?
      "action_id": "-1",
      "action_text": "CLICK",
      "params": {"coordinates": []} # TODO definir formato das coordenadas
    },
    {
      "action_id": "3",
      "action_text": "SET_TEXT (3)",
      "params": {"text": "text generated by LLM"}
    }
    // Additional related actions...
  ]
}


DO NOT include any additional text outside of the JSON object. Your response must be valid JSON that can be parsed directly.
